# Files two engine jobs both write that no driver above merges: a guide's or a breed's pictures, an album, a playlist, a
# page's summary card, the photo review page. Until 16 Nov they merged line by line, and the push fallback (`git pull
# --rebase -X theirs`) gave a part photo another photo's credit, and a still another still's caption and "no one in it"
# mark (8, 9, 15 and 16 Nov 2026). Now no record is built from two versions: main's file, with what the run took off
# taken off and what it put in put in, each record whole; a summary card main's whole, unless the run took main's
# approved card back to pending (scripts/merge-main-whole.mjs). Only the engine's clones set this driver (the job
# scripts); elsewhere (leads' checkouts, GitHub's merges) these merge as text, as before. Not the pages' language files:
# main's file there would drop a hold the run added, and their holds follow main_holds (scripts/cycle-checks.sh).
content/guides/*/entity.json merge=main-whole
content/breeds/*/entity.json merge=main-whole
content/gallery/*.json merge=main-whole
content/series/*.json merge=main-whole
content/summaries/*.json merge=main-whole
